      <div type="clause" n="19">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 19</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>XVII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.5"/> Gif hwa his wæpnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.6"/> oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> onlæne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.7"/>, þæt he mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.8"/> mid ófslea, hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.9"/> moton hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.10"/> gesomnian, gif hie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.10"/> willað, to þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.11"/> were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>XVII. Gif hwa his wæpn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.5-2"/> oðrum læne, ðæt he mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.2"/> mid ofslea, hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.1"/> moton hy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.1"/> gesomnian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.2"/>, gif hi willað, to ðæm were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="60" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe heore wepna lenað to manslihte. Gyf hwa his wæpne oðrum læne, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he mid man ofslea, hi moton hi g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>sa<hi rend="italic">m</hi>nian, gyf hí wyllað, to ðæm were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis alteri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.8-2"/> prestet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.9-2"/> arma sua in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.10-2"/> occisione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.11-2"/> alicuius, licet eis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.12"/>, si uelint, weram eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_19.lnote.oe.13"/>(mortui) coniectare.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe heore wepna lenað to manslihte.] Gif hwa his wæpnes oðrum onlæne<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Af_19.attnote.fn.19"/>, þæt he mon mid ófslea, hie moton hie gesomnian gif hie willað, to þam were.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="22" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="312" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XVII} Gif hwa his wæpnes oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> onlæne, þæt he mon mid ófslea, hie moton hie gesomnian gif hie willað, to þam were.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="61" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer einem anderen seine Waffe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_19.lnote.de.1"/> hinleiht, womit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_19.lnote.de.2"/> der einen Menschen erschlägt, so dürfen sie, wenn sie wollen, sich zusammenthun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_19.lnote.de.3"/> zur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_19.lnote.de.4"/> Wergeld[bezahlung].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone lends his weapon to another, with which the latter slays a person, they may, if they wish, join together for [payment of] the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="73" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone lends a weapon of his to another [man], for the purpose of committing murder with it, they<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_19.attnote.n.1"/> may, if they are willing to, combine to pay the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone lends his weapon to another that he may kill a man with it, they may, if they wish, join to pay the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="313" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone loans his weapon to another so that he can kill a man, they may combine to pay the <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> if they want to.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_18">Abt 18–20</ref> <quote>a lender's liability for any blood spilt by the weapon loaned (n. 86: Af 19 – 19:3; Abt 18 – 20)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt nach</hi> 17 <hi rend="italic">So; nach</hi> 18 <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">follows after 17 in So; after 18 in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wæpne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wæpne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">læne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">læne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mid man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mid man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">dahinter 2 Buchst. radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">after it 2 letters erased</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ó <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ó altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">60</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Lond, fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only Lond, lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">marito [<hi rend="italic">aus vor. Zeile</hi>] <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> pr. ar., <hi rend="italic">darunter im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.:</hi> arma <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">marito [from the previous line] instead of pr. ar., below it in the 16th cent.: arma R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond,</hi> occidendum aliquem <hi rend="italic">R</hi> (<hi rend="italic">wo aber</hi> quem <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi>) <hi rend="italic">T Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; occidendum aliquem R (where, however, quem is on an erasure) T Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei si uelit <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei si uelit Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> e. <hi rend="italic">Lond, nur</hi> m. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only e. Lond, only m. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Genetiv von ‘leihen’ abhängend; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 30. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Beihilfe 10. Als Beweggrund zum Entleihen der Waffe denkt an den Wunsch, den Ursprung des Totschlags zu verbergen Pol Mai I 31; die Kostbarkeit der Waffen aber genügt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Genitive dependent on ‘lend’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 30. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Beihilfe 10. Pol Mai I 31 supposes the motive for borrowing the weapon to be the wish to conceal the origin of the homicide; but the costliness of weapons is a sufficient explanation</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bessere Übs.: ‘dass der damit’; so wohl Q. Dagegen ‘<hi rend="italic">inde</hi>’ schrieb Inst. (wie früher ich ‘womit’), weil <hi rend="italic">þæt</hi> als Rel., abhängig von Präp. <hi rend="italic">mid</hi> genommen wurde, wie in Af 21 und <hi rend="italic">þone ele þæt þu myd</hi> (Öl, womit du) <hi rend="italic">smyrian mote,</hi> bei Toller 684b XII</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Better transl.: ‘that he with it’; so probably Q. Inst., on the other hand, wrote ‘<hi rend="italic">inde</hi>’ (as I formerly wrote ‘with which’), because <hi rend="italic">þæt</hi> was taken as a rel. dependent on the prep. <hi rend="italic">mid</hi>, as in Af 21 and <hi rend="italic">þone ele þæt þu myd</hi> (the oil with which you) <hi rend="italic">smyrian mote,</hi> in Toller 684b XII</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘zusammenschiessen’ Q; ‘sich vereinigen’ Schmid. Hier liegt private Abmachung vor, im Ggs. zur gesetzlichen Beitragspflicht wegen Beihilfe in 19, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘to club together’ Q; ‘to unite’ Schmid. What is meant here is a private agreement, in contrast to the statutory duty to contribute on account of aiding and abetting in 19, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_19.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Anders Kents Recht; s. Beihilfe 10b. Hier kann also schon (im Ggs. zu früherem Formalismus) die Haftung (<hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 4c) für Eine Tat mehrere solidarisch treffen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Kent’s law is different; see Beihilfe 10b. Here, then (in contrast to earlier formalism), liability (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 4c) for a single deed can already fall jointly and severally on several persons</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_19.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>onlæne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">læne</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_19.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">195</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the lender and the borrower.</seg></note>
      </div>
